Here is the summary of the infrastructure and configuration files we explicitly fixed:

core/config.py: Refactored the Pydantic model to enforce standard DB defaults (port 5432, enterprise_rag_db). Added URL-encoding to DB_PASSWORD to prevent parsing exceptions with special characters like @. Wired ProductionConfig to read .env.production for local proxy migrations.

Dockerfile.backend & Dockerfile.frontend: Updated the CMD entrypoints to use dynamic  injection. This guarantees the containers can run locally on 8000/8501, while seamlessly binding to the dynamic ports required by serverless GCP Cloud Run.

docker-compose.staging.yml: Removed conflicting DOCKER_DB_HOST variables. Set internal networking to use standard staging-db:5432 DNS routing, while mapping the host port to 5434 to prevent local Windows conflicts.

infra/variables.tf: Defined the strict canonical variables (db_name, db_user, app_env) so Terraform stops relying on default PostgreSQL values.

infra/main.tf: Mapped the Cloud SQL instance and Cloud Run container directly to the new canonical variables. Injected APP_ENV=PRODUCTION explicitly into the container runtime.

storage/db_seeder.py: Refactored the insert_staged_vector_batch function to drop explicit ID insertion, allowing PostgreSQL to correctly handle its own auto-incrementing native sequences.
